r familiar locales that should make  star wars aficionados ears perk the  mention of scar F is about much more  than letting us know it's still intact  in the timeline of solo it also  reaffirms just how gutsy the events of  rogue 1 really were the planet is  mentioned by Kira as a possible source  of some replacement Co axiom after the  team muffs their first attempt to boost  some from a train on Vandor one scarf is  quickly passed over because of the heavy  security surrounding the planet and the  group instead opts to risk the Kessel  run with unstable explosives rather than  even take a chance at scar F in other  words jyn erso and her little band of  rebels were even braver than we knew  the seeds of rebellion the first  stand-alone Star Wars story rogue one  was basically a feature-length tribute  to some of the previously unknown heroes  that help feel the rebellion that would  ultimately topple an empire by getting  those Death Star plans into Leia's hands  solo on the other hand is focused on the  history and character development of the  galaxy's most lovable rogue and proves  he was known to act unselfishly on at  least one occasion prior to saving Luke  Skywalker from Darth Vader squadron of  TIE fighters what it means for Han to  betray dryden vos and deliver the  precious fuel to emphasis ragtag team is  fairly epic before he was ready to align  with anyone who'd fill his pockets but  now he has scruples and guts and fists  nest else on that the co axiom is the  blood of a new rebellion in other words  long before Han would ever meet Luke and  obi-wan at the cantina he'd already  begun his work aiding the Rebel Alliance  let the wookie win some references are a  little more obscure than others like  when Lando Calrissian uses his downtime  to chronicle his adventures via hologram  and makes mention of the alien race the  shahru this is a major nod to the novel  Lando Calrissian and the mind harp of  charu which hasn't been considered canon  but offers